{#-
  Lagoon — approve + NAV settlement and operations on a single Lagoon vault.

  ONE vault per config. Pass the RESOLVED vault contract address (a literal
  `0x…` string or `{{ aliases.lagoon.<key> }}`) — the template does no
  further lookup on the vault, as Lagoon vaults are case-specific and the
  registry ships no globals. The `asset`, by contrast, is a TOKEN ALIAS KEY
  (e.g. "USDC") resolved via aliases.tokens[<key>] INSIDE the template — the
  same way aave_v3 / compound_v3 / ondo_* take their deposit/payment assets.

  Required template params:
    vault — the 0x-prefixed Lagoon vault contract address.
    asset — the token alias KEY of the vault's underlying (the vault's
            `asset()`), e.g. "USDC". Resolved via aliases.tokens[<asset>]
            with NO existence guard ⇒ render-time error if missing. The role
            is granted approve(spender = vault, amount = *) on this token ONLY.
    safe_is_valuation_manager — bool. Whether the Safe is the vault's
            `valuationManager`. `true` additionally grants
            updateNewTotalAssets (propose a NAV). `false` leaves it out:
            the vault only accepts that call from its valuationManager, so
            on a vault whose valuationManager is another address the grant
            could never be exercised through the Roles modifier. Required
            rather than defaulted, and asserted as a YAML boolean, so each
            config states the vault's setup instead of inheriting a grant
            that is either inert or, if the vault is later reconfigured,
            unreviewed authority to propose the NAV the same role settles.

  Resolved from aliases (NOT passed as a raw address):
    aliases.tokens[asset] — the underlying ERC-20 the vault pulls on deposit.

  Output shape:
    - One approve role on the resolved asset token: erc20.approve(spender,
      amount) with the spender pinned to `vault` (equal_to) and amount left
      `pass`. This lets the Safe authorize the vault to pull its underlying
      on deposit, and authorize nothing else — the spender is hard-scoped to
      the vault, and approve on any other token is not granted.
    - One vault role on `vault`, with five allowed functions (six with
      `safe_is_valuation_manager: true`), all execution_options: "none".
      Every parameter is declared `pass` explicitly (zac's validator
      requires every signature param to be covered); the all-pass
      optimization in `toSdkTargets` then collapses this to `allowFunction`
      on-chain.
    - Functions covered (see Lagoon docs §Smart-Contract Reference):
      • updateNewTotalAssets(uint256)     — propose a new NAV value
                                            (only with safe_is_valuation_manager)
      • settleDeposit(uint256)            — confirm NAV + settle pending deposits
      • settleRedeem(uint256)             — confirm NAV + settle pending redemptions
      • expireTotalAssets()               — force the current NAV value to expire
      • claimSharesOnBehalf(address[])    — push minted shares to depositors post-settlement
      • claimAssetsOnBehalf(address[])    — push redeemed assets to redeemers post-settlement

    `updateTotalAssetsLifespan(uint128)` is NOT granted, on any vault.

    On an async-only vault the omission costs nothing: `activateAsyncOnly()`
    shuts the setter, and the call reverts `AsyncOnly()` (0x9c960ece) when the
    vault's safe makes it. Guard order matters if you probe this — `onlySafe`
    is checked first, so any other caller gets `OnlySafe(safe)` (0xfde82f1f)
    and never reaches the async check.

    On a vault where async-only has not been activated the setter is live and
    succeeds from the safe, so the omission withholds authority that exists.
    That is intended: `totalAssetsLifespan` governs how long a settled NAV
    stays valid, and the role that settles the NAV should not also set how
    long it is trusted. The role can only ever shorten that window, via
    `expireTotalAssets()`. And the permission is withheld from the ROLE, not
    from the safe — the vault gates the setter on `onlySafe`, so the safe
    keeps it through a direct owner transaction.

  Settlement on the vault (v0.6.0) is a two-step flow: the vault's
  valuationManager proposes a NAV via updateNewTotalAssets(x), then the
  vault's safe confirms it by calling settleDeposit(x) / settleRedeem(x)
  with the SAME value — the vault reverts on a mismatch or when no
  proposal is pending. updateNewTotalAssets only executes through the
  Roles modifier when the Safe itself is the vault's valuationManager,
  which is what `safe_is_valuation_manager` declares.
-#}
{%- from "_macros/common.tmpl" import approve -%}
{#- Assert the flag is a real boolean before gating on it: a quoted "false" is a
    non-empty string, which nunjucks treats as truthy. -#}
{%- set safe_is_valuation_manager = safe_is_valuation_manager | bool("safe_is_valuation_manager") -%}
# safe_is_valuation_manager: {{ safe_is_valuation_manager }}
roles:
  {{ approve(aliases.tokens[asset], vault) | indent(2) }}

  - address: "{{ vault }}"
    functions:
{%- if safe_is_valuation_manager %}
      - signature: "function updateNewTotalAssets(uint256 _newTotalAssets)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: _newTotalAssets
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"
{% endif %}
      - signature: "function settleDeposit(uint256 _newTotalAssets)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: _newTotalAssets
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"

      - signature: "function settleRedeem(uint256 _newTotalAssets)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: _newTotalAssets
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"

      - signature: "function expireTotalAssets()"
        execution_options: "none"

      - signature: "function claimSharesOnBehalf(address[] controllers)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: controllers
            param_type: "dynamic"
            operator: "pass"

      - signature: "function claimAssetsOnBehalf(address[] controllers)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: controllers
            param_type: "dynamic"
            operator: "pass"
